<title>LEBANON: Mexico reopens Lebanon embassy.</title>
<headline>Mexico reopens Lebanon embassy.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-11-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico became the latest country to reopen its embassy in Beirut after a long shutdown caused by Lebanon's 1975-90 civil war.</p>
<p>The new Mexican ambassador, Edgardo Flores Rivas, presented his credentials on Friday to President Elias Hrawi.</p>
<p>A statement issued by the embassy said Mexico has about 500,000 citizens of Lebanese origin.</p>
</text>
